    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is heavily impacted by off-days, forcing Ghost Ride the WHIP to rely on a concentrated group to secure our counting stats. **Brice Turang** stands as our premier play at 67.53, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez. With an xERA of 4.63, Martinez presents a soft landing for **Brice Turang**, whose profile is bolstered by a 15% skill-adjustment for the matchup and a move up to the #5 spot in the order. His elite speed profile remains our primary engine for SB accumulation, making him a must-start regardless of the surrounding roster vacancies. While the remainder of our core\u2014including power hitters like **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2014are sidelined due to schedule gaps, the efficiency of **Brice Turang** provides a stable floor for the day.\n\nThe optimization process for today was largely dictated by the lack of viable alternatives, as the schedule keeps our high-ceiling talent like **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** on the bench. Among those inactive, **Corbin Carroll** and **Jose Caballero** represent the biggest losses to our daily SB production, as their absence removes our primary engine for disrupting the base paths. We are also monitoring the availability of prospects like **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** to see if late-season call-ups might bridge the gap during these quiet stretches; however, for today, we are effectively in a holding pattern. We continue to hold **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, and **Dalton Rushing** in reserve, waiting for the schedule to align so we can deploy our full offensive arsenal again. No weather risks are currently flagging, but the limited volume of play makes maximizing the efficiency of **Brice Turang** our sole priority.",
